# Global preferences

## Response style
- Keep explanations concise — lead with the answer, add context below
- Use conventional commit format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`
- Show the terminal command to verify changes when relevant
- Prefer composition over inheritance

## Code conventions
- Nullable reference types enabled by default — always handle nulls explicitly
- Async all the way down — no `.Result` or `.Wait()` calls
- Named exports; no wildcard re-exports

## Commit & PR
- Commit subject ≤ 72 characters, imperative mood ("Add X" not "Added X")
- PR title matches the commit subject
- Every PR references a GitHub issue number
